This is an independent opt-in extension to MiaAI-Lab's DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017
recipe, not an official MiaAI, TensorFold, DeepSeek or NVIDIA release.

Original work and notices are retained in:
  licenses/MiaAI-NOTICE
  licenses/MiaAI-CREDITS.md
  licenses/TensorFold-NOTICE
  licenses/TensorFold-THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
  licenses/tensorfold/

Changes in this extension (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)):
  patches/9999-cache-io-backpressure.patch modifies
    zig/src/core/lane_host.zig
    zig/src/core/lane_host_tier_test.zig
  It adds a default-off host admission gate for long image prefills while cache
  I/O is pending, bounded by the existing load-wait policy, plus eight CPU tests.
  The patch adds prominent module-documentation modification notices to both files.
  The runtime and test bodies match the measured implementation; those notice
  comments are the only source difference introduced for public distribution.

  patches/9999-shared-prefix-checkpoint.patch modifies
    zig/src/server/chat.zig
    zig/src/server/openai.zig
  and adds
    zig/src/server/shared_checkpoint.zig
    zig/src/server/response_timing.zig
  It adds a default-off aligned shared-prefix checkpoint before volatile client
  metadata, optional metadata-only first-stream-event timing, and helper tests.
  Two prominent module-documentation notice lines are prepended to each file;
  runtime and test bodies otherwise match the measured implementation.
  Existing TensorFold prefix caching, spill storage and model math are unchanged.

The preparation tools, portable synthetic workloads, result extraction and
explanatory documentation are additions to this extension. They do not replace
or claim authorship of the model, quantization, engine, kernels, RDMA transport,
spill store, parked-restore machinery, or existing prefill interleave.

No weights, kernel binaries, credentials or private service controllers are
redistributed. Third-party code quoted as patch context retains its license.
